Fix SM90 backward accumulator layout in flash-attn-4 4.0.0b19.
The interface and dQ postprocess round heads to 32, so the main backward
kernel must use the same head stride. A head of 72 otherwise writes an
80-wide layout that postprocess reads as 96-wide, corrupting dQ.
Already 32-aligned heads retain their original tile sizes.

--- a/flash_attn/cute/flash_bwd_sm90.py
+++ b/flash_attn/cute/flash_bwd_sm90.py
@@ -76,8 +76,8 @@
         dQ_single_wg: bool = False,
     ):
         self.dtype = dtype
-        # padding head_dim to a multiple of 16 as k_block_size
-        hdim_multiple_of = 16
+        # Match the 32-element head stride of the FP32 accumulator and postprocess.
+        hdim_multiple_of = 32
         self.tile_hdim = int(math.ceil(head_dim / hdim_multiple_of) * hdim_multiple_of)
         head_dim_v = head_dim_v if head_dim_v is not None else head_dim
         self.same_hdim_kv = head_dim == head_dim_v
